  "question": {
    "text": "A boy of mass $40 \\mathrm{~kg}$ is climbing a vertical pole at a constant speed. If the coefficient of friction between his palms and the pole is 0.8 and $g=10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2$, the horizontal force that he is applying on the pole is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "EV622",
      "text": "$300 \\mathrm{~N}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "fYcR3",
      "text": "$400 \\mathrm{~N}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "dxTUF",
      "text": "$500 \\mathrm{~N}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "K1azn",
      "text": "$600 \\mathrm{~N}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hints: Here $\\mu=0.8$\nFrictional force $=\\mu \\mathrm{N}_1=m g$\n$$\n\\mathrm{N}_1=\\frac{m g}{\\mu}=\\frac{400}{0.8}=500 \\mathrm{~N}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
